# Research Reproducibility

- Drive experiments from version-controlled configuration files under
  `configs/`; do not hide hyperparameters in source code.
- Record the code version, `uv.lock`, configuration, seed set, player count,
  observation/reward choices, opponents, and output location.
- Keep training opponents separate from known and previously unseen evaluation
  opponents when measuring generalization.
- Use bounded smoke runs before expensive training or tournaments.
- Preserve machine-readable results and enough metadata to reproduce them.
- Report game win rate plus relevant secondary metrics from
  `docs/requirements-and-scope.md`.
- Keep checkpoints, logs, datasets, and metrics out of Git unless deliberately
  curated.
